export anchor CartographicStyle:
    number: 71
    screen: TodayMobile
    name: Cartographic
    idea: The day is drawn as a survey map on contour-lined paper, with tasks as stops along a dashed route, meetings as waypoints and a legend for every marker.
    base: light
    palette:
        land: #f2f0e4, the page outside the map
        surveyPaper: #fbfaf3, the map sheet, cards and the legend
        contour: #cfd3b4, contour lines, decorative only
        water: #d6e7ec, the lake shape, the avatar and the active nav disc
        surveyInk: #24301f, text, frames and the compass
        moss: #545d48, meta text and upcoming rings
        boundary: #7d8466, card and field borders
        routeRed: #b0331f, the route line, the overdue triangle, the add button and focus
        pinBlue: #1e5a7a, due today pins and meeting diamonds
        forest: #2f6b3a, the done flag and tick
    type:
        Serif italic Georgia, Iowan Old Style, Palatino Linotype, serif for
        place-like names, 26px for the date, 15px for project and meeting
        names. Humanist sans Gill Sans, Gill Sans MT, Optima, Candara,
        Segoe UI, system-ui for everything else, with 16px semibold task
        names, 20px semibold tabular meeting times, 13px meta, and 10 to
        12px semibold caps labels tracked 0.24 to 0.36em.
    layout:
        A framed map sheet up to 400px wide centred on the land colour, with
        a double frame. Faint contour lines, a pale lake shape and a dotted
        survey grid fill the background. A title cartouche with a double
        frame holds the brand, the date, 6 tasks, 2 meetings and a round
        avatar with a dashed ring. A scale bar reading 1 day and a small
        compass rose follow. Waypoints shows the two meetings as side by
        side cards with a diamond, time, name and length. The route lists
        the six tasks with a 36px marker column joined by a dashed red line
        and a card for each stop. A legend box explains every marker, then
        the bottom bar sits under a rule with a raised round red add button.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 8px between stops, 10px between waypoint cards, 24px before region labels.
    density: Medium. Each stop is two short lines.
    corners: Square frames and cards. The avatar, badge, add button and pill buttons are round.
    borders: 1px boundary lines on cards. The map and cartouche have double frames with a 3 to 4px gap. The overdue card gets a 2px route red border.
    shadows: None. Depth comes from frames and the contour paper.
    icons:
        Map markers show status by shape, a blue teardrop pin for Due today,
        a hollow ring for Upcoming, a green flag for Done and a red triangle
        with an exclamation mark for Overdue. Meetings use blue diamonds.
        Every marker also has a word beside it. Nav icons are thin 1.6
        stroke map symbols such as a compass and a folded map.
    focus: A 2px dashed route red outline offset 3px.
    tone: Gentle surveyor words for headings, such as Waypoints, The route and Legend. Item text stays plain.
